{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Melchizedek.</b> He is called thus because he is king over the place of righteousness. Some say that it is a name." "And Shalem is Jerusalem, as witness: \"His abode is in Shalem\" (Psalms 76:3)." "<b>And he was priest.</b> As the Aramaic translator rendered, and so every priest, as witness: \"and he shall minister to Me\" (Exodus 28:41). And the meaning of \"after the manner of Melchizedek\" in the Book of Praises (Psalms 110:4) is that he spoke fittingly and did well, for he blessed Abram first because he volunteered to rescue those who were taken captive, and afterward he said, \"and blessed is HaShem,\" who helped him and delivered his enemies into his hands."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:36.224263419Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}